WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
- As Hispanic Heritage
Month comes to a close,

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.380
I want to introduce a
group of women shattering

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.640
the glass ceiling in the male
dominated world of mariachi.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.010
Their goal is to keep this
traditional Mexican music alive

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.810
while adding a touch of femininity.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.680
From Sacramento, California, give it up

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.130
for Dinorah, Janessa,
Audra, Jordan and Samantha.

00:00:19.068 --> 00:00:21.004
Mariachi Bonitas!

00:00:21.004 --> 00:00:24.337
(mariachi music begins)

00:00:25.374 --> 00:00:30.374
(Mariachi Bonitas singing
in foreign language)

00:00:46.775 --> 00:00:48.532
(mariachi music ends)

00:00:48.532 --> 00:00:51.532
(audience cheering)

00:00:52.403 --> 00:00:53.486
Come on over.

00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:57.951
Oh my god!

00:00:57.951 --> 00:00:59.144
I loved it!

00:00:59.144 --> 00:01:00.568
It's nice to meet you.

00:01:00.568 --> 00:01:01.682
- It's nice to meet you, Kelly.

00:01:01.682 --> 00:01:03.278
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:03.278 --> 00:01:04.568
Have a seat.

00:01:04.568 --> 00:01:05.401
- Thank you.

00:01:05.401 --> 00:01:07.330
- Oh my god, it sounds so beautiful.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.740
I grew up singing a harmony
with like a bunch of girls too.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.420
It's just the blend is so nice.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.740
- Thank you so much. - It's so beautiful.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.920
- I don't know if everybody's met.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.790
But meet Hasan and Malia.
- Yes. Hello, hi.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.803
- I grew up near Sacramento. Davis.

00:01:18.753 --> 00:01:21.587
(audience cheering)

00:01:21.587 --> 00:01:22.638
- He's like represent.

00:01:22.638 --> 00:01:23.471
- Yes, very well.

00:01:23.471 --> 00:01:25.700
- Well, I want to share a little bit,

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:26.990
a little bit more about the lyrics

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:27.823
of what you were saying.

00:01:27.823 --> 00:01:29.120
So they're translating in English

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.697
and it's "beautiful are the
women of my beloved Mexico.

00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:34.327
"Beautiful are it's songs,

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.947
"it's valleys and mountains.

00:01:35.947 --> 00:01:38.857
"Beautiful are the stars
that shine upon its beaches,

00:01:38.857 --> 00:01:41.227
"and Mariachi Bonitas sing with joy

00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:42.550
"to our beautiful country."

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.990
That's so cool.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.060
- Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.300
- I wanted everybody to
know what you're singing.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.470
So you wrote that song, right?
- I did, I did.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:53.610
- Okay so why, why is a song
like this so important to you?

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.000
- Well I wanted to have, for us to have

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.440
a theme that not only
represent us as women.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.520
Like you say, Mariachi
Bonitas is very feminine.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.370
That's representing what we are.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.940
But not only that is, is to

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.470
give a tribute, pay a
tribute to the culture,

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.480
to our music, to our art.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.870
That is so, so us, you know.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.480
And being far away from Mexico

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.640
well of course you have
to, have that in you

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.000
and in, in playing this song makes us

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.918
just have Mexico in our hearts, you know.

00:02:23.918 --> 00:02:24.751
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:24.751 --> 00:02:25.584
- Closer to us.

00:02:25.584 --> 00:02:27.970
And now being all females as well,

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:31.020
we can be a little, you
know, sassy and feminine

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.973
and so, we can get away with that.

00:02:32.973 --> 00:02:33.806
- You bring something different.

00:02:33.806 --> 00:02:35.050
Yeah, I love that.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.440
Well, Audra and Jordan, why
did you want to join in?

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.700
What does it mean to you
to be a part of the group?

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.760
- [Audra] Well I've been,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.100
I've been playing the
violin for over 16 years

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.960
and I was a high school Spanish teacher.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.010
And I saw a huge decline
in knowledge of mariachi.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.240
They thought it was all the same thing.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.440
I was like, no man,
this is beautiful stuff.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.416
So I, you know, I cooperate with lessons.

00:02:55.416 --> 00:02:56.900
But more than that,

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.520
I really wanted to empower the females

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.670
in my high school that I was teaching at.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:04.420
And just in general that you
don't see that many females

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.790
in mariachi world.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.550
- I've never seen it until today.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:08.383
Honest to God.

00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:09.216
That's why I was like,

00:03:09.216 --> 00:03:10.210
when I was so excited
about y'all coming on,

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.410
I was like, I have seen
a lot of mariachi bands,

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.630
I feel like in my lifetime

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.470
and I've never seen a female in it.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.699
So I thought it was so cool.

00:03:16.699 --> 00:03:17.532
- [Audra] Yeah.

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:18.884
- [Kelly] Well, Jordan, how about you?

00:03:18.884 --> 00:03:21.480
(audience clapping)

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.740
- I saw her post on Facebook
and I am not Hispanic,

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.930
but I have played in orchestras.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.110
I've played in jazz bands and operas

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.060
and I thought, I'm going to do it.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.060
I'm going to try it, I'm
going to see what it's like.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.400
And I started, it was,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.390
it was a little bit rough of a start,

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.500
but we practiced every
week. It's so much fun.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.290
The culture, I've completely
embraced the culture.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.730
It is a family everywhere we go.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.400
We've played gigs where they feed us.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.740
They're dancing and singing.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.950
And it is so much fun.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.650
I've never experienced
anything like this before.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.860
- See I kind of loved
your story from this.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.087
Like I was,

00:03:56.087 --> 00:03:57.020
(mumbles)

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.700
reading last night about you in the group.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.560
And I was like, I love that like,

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.610
everybody always thinks
that you have to be like,

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.680
oh you have to be Mexican to like this.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:04.600
I'm like, no, you don't.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.250
You don't have to be any kind of color,

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.400
walk a lot to like any
kind of music or anything.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.360
And I think that that's really cool.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.280
The other little girls see
that as an opportunity as well.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.113
- [Jordan] Yeah.

00:04:14.113 --> 00:04:14.946
- So it's really cool what you're doing.

00:04:14.946 --> 00:04:16.768
It's beautiful music, I love it.

00:04:16.768 --> 00:04:17.601
- [Female Mariachi's]
Thank you, thank you.

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:18.434
- [Kelly] It's so beautiful

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.380
But Sammy, what about you?

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.050
- Well, I started in high school.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.010
I got out of high school

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.200
and I was gigging professionally,
like with other musicians,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.430
and then Dinorah contacted
me about the all girl group

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.590
and I was like, yeah, why not, you know?

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.010
I think it's really important
that we're an all girl group

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.900
because traditionally it's all men.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.733
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:38.566
- [Sammy] You know, and we're like, bam!

00:04:38.566 --> 00:04:39.940
in your face, you know, like.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.320
(group laughing)

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.480
So, yeah, that.
- I love that.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.313
That's so cool.

00:04:44.313 --> 00:04:45.650
And what a cool sisterhood too,

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.097
to like, share like in that that's cool.

00:04:47.097 --> 00:04:48.070
- [Sammy] Yeah, these are my homies.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.027
- Yeah, that's so good.

00:04:49.027 --> 00:04:52.040
That's so good. And Janessa,
you're the youngest, right?

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:52.873
- Yes, I am.

00:04:52.873 --> 00:04:55.000
- [Kelly] So, so I mean,
what do you love about it?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.550
- Yeah, so I'm 17 years old

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.120
and music has always been my passion.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.090
I believe I got my love for
music from my grandfather.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.560
He is a Colombian composer.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.530
Unfortunately, he passed last year.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.750
However, being able to
be a part of this band

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.200
let's me be close to him,
let's me connect with him

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.470
and as well, let's me be able
to connect with my heritage.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.060
And of course being a part
of this group gives me

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.870
it's, it's an amazing experience

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.430
and it's an amazing opportunity

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.130
to be with such a
wonderful group of ladies.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:21.963
- Beautiful.

00:05:21.963 --> 00:05:24.250
And you actually, Malia,
you're working hard right now

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.080
to help women get their
voices heard right now,

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:26.913
as well right?

00:05:26.913 --> 00:05:29.270
- Yeah, I'm co-hosting #GirlHero Awards

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.890
on October 14th and I
just feel really honored

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.530
to be a part of such an
incredible community for sure.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:35.363
- Absolutely.

00:05:35.363 --> 00:05:37.593
Yes, stand up for each other.

